# Sync experiment documentation

When you change experiment config or commit new baselines, **update experimentDocs in the same task**.

## Doc split

| File | Contents |
|------|----------|
| **`experimentDocs/EXPERIMENTS.md`** | Live LLM tests (Gemini API) — real MSAs, task outcomes, real-world examples |
| **`experimentDocs/MOCK_EXPERIMENTS.md`** | Mock baseline + ablations — CI, simulated agents, no API |
| **`experimentDocs/FINDINGS.md`** | Interpretation (live-first; link to mock doc) |

## Triggers

- `benchmark/run_live_experiment.py`, `benchmark/live_providers.py` → update **EXPERIMENTS.md**, FINDINGS.md
- `benchmark/experiment.py`, `benchmark/run_ablations.py` → update **MOCK_EXPERIMENTS.md**
- Committed `experiments/*/results.json` → update the matching doc + FINDINGS if interpretation changes

## Checklist

1. `experimentDocs/EXPERIMENTS.md` — live runs, real-life scenarios, per-task Gemini outcomes
2. `experimentDocs/MOCK_EXPERIMENTS.md` — mock/ablation matrices and CI summaries
3. `experimentDocs/FINDINGS.md` — live interpretation
4. `README.md` — link live doc first; mock doc second
5. `context/STORE.md` — status + decisions log
6. Bump `Last synced` dates in both catalog files

## Verification

```powershell
python scripts/sync_experiment_docs.py --check
python -m pytest tests/ -q
```

Do not paste API keys into committed files.
